    "id": "Prob062_bugs_mux2",
    "spec": "\r\nConsider the following implementation of an 8-bit 2-to-1 mux:\r\n\r\n  module TopModule (\r\n      input        sel,\r\n      input  [7:0] a,\r\n      input  [7:0] b,\r\n      output       out\r\n  );\r\n\r\n      assign out = (~sel & a) | (sel & b);\r\n\r\n  endmodule\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, this module has a bug. Implement a new version of this\r\nmodule that fixes the bug.\r\n\r\n",
    "interface": {
      "top": "TopModule",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "sel",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "a",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 8,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "b",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 8,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "out",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 8,
          "signed": false
        }
      ]
    },
    "constraints": "SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI.\nPublic interface erratum (p10-public-interface-062-v1): The public prompt requires an 8-bit 2-to-1 mux, but its buggy example declares out as one bit. Interpret out as an eight-bit output; sel remains a one-bit input and a and b remain eight-bit inputs. This approved interface correction overrides only that output-width typo; the original prompt is preserved."
  },
  "sample_id": "f1c93d4c-2aad-44d2-ac01-c0af2fe07320",
  "variant_id": "C",
  "current": {
    "revision_id": "c0caf851-01dd-4f2e-8a53-b3b7d0c3f06d",
